# No em dashes or en dashes

Do not use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`) in UI copy, comments, docs, prompts, or commit messages.

Use ordinary punctuation instead:

- Parenthetical asides: commas or parentheses
- Breaks between clauses: a period or semicolon
- Definitions or labels: a colon only when introducing what follows
- Numeric or letter ranges: a hyphen (`1-5`, `A-B`)
- Empty / missing placeholders in UI: a hyphen (`-`)

Parsers may still *match* em/en dashes in model output so external text remains parseable. Do not *author* those characters.
